# {{title}}

An Umbel compiled plugin: a Rust crate linked into a host binary. It has one command,
`{{id}}-hello`, one pack, `starter`, and one skill, `{{id}}-guide`.

```sh
cargo test                      # the plugin through the test kit
umbel plugin check path=.       # the manifest, grants, schemas, packs and skills
```

`Cargo.toml` names two path or git dependencies, `umbel-sdk` and `umbel`. Point them at your
checkout of `endpoints/umbel` if you work from one.

To run it, link it into a binary: call `umbel::cli::run` with a `configure` hook that adds
`umbel::plugins::sdk({{lib}}::plugin())` through `HostBuilder::with_compiled`, then enable it in
`umbel.toml` with `plugins.enabled = ["{{id}}"]` and `plugins.{{id}}.source = "compiled:{{id}}"`.

A compiled plugin runs with the host's own permissions. The grants in `umbel-plugin.toml` say what
it uses; they do not sandbox it. Build it as a component (`umbel plugin new kind=component`) when
it must run untrusted.
